raph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(The words of a talebearer are as wounds,¦layout ‚¤textÙ7And they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤text¿Burning lips and a wicked heart¦layout ‚¤textÙ.Are like a potsherd covered with silver dross.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ)He that hateth dissembleth with his lips,¦layout ‚¤textÙ And layeth up deceit within him;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'When he speaketh fair, believe him not:¦layout ‚¤textÙ.For there are seven abominations in his heart.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"Whose hatred is covered by deceit,¦layout ‚¤textÙ=His wickedness shall be shewed before the whole congregation.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'Whoso diggeth a pit shall fall therein:¦layout ‚¤textÙ5And he that rolleth a stone, it will return upon him.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ5A lying tongue hateth those that are afflicted by it;¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And a flattering mouth worketh ruin.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse